    "body": "## Overview\n\n`vllm run-batch` accepts `--tool-parser-plugin` and `--reasoning-parser-plugin` but never imports them, so a parser registered by a plugin can't be used in batch mode. `vllm serve` imports both in `setup_server`, and #53124 did the same for `--headless`; `run-batch` is the entrypoint that was left out.\n\n## Claims\n\n- `run_batch.main` imports the tool and reasoning parser plugins before it validates the args and builds the engine config, in the same order as the API server.\n\n## Validation\n\nWith a plugin file that registers `my_reasoner` (a subclass of the DeepSeek R1 parser):\n\n```console\n$ vllm run-batch -i in.jsonl -o out.jsonl --model Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B \\\n    --reasoning-parser my_reasoner --reasoning-parser-plugin /path/to/my_reasoning_plugin.py\n  File \"vllm/config/reasoning.py\", line 84, in initialize_token_ids\n  File \"vllm/reasoning/abs_reasoning_parsers.py\", line 247, in get_reasoning_parser\nKeyError: \"Reasoning parser 'my_reasoner' not found. Available parsers: cohere_command3, ...\"\n```\n\nWith the change the same command gets past config creation and reaches `Initializing a V1 LLM engine`.\n\nThe new test in `tests/entrypoints/launchers/test_run_batch.py` writes two small plugin files, parses real `run-batch` arguments and checks that both parsers are registered by the time the engine client is built. On main it fails with `AssertionError: assert 'batch_plugin_tool' in [...]`.\n\n```\npytest tests/entrypoints/launchers/test_run_batch.py -k \"plugins or download or upload or transcription_wrapper\"\nruff check && ruff format --check   # on the two touched files\n```\n\nBoth pass locally. This was a CPU-only box, so the tests in that file that spawn `vllm run-batch` with real weights were not run, and the engine in the manual run above did not finish starting.\n\n## Details\n\nNoticed while reading the plugin-loading call sites. The tool parser half fails later than the reasoning one: nothing looks the tool parser up until the chat handler is built, so `--enable-auto-tool-choice --tool-call-parser my_tool --tool-parser-plugin ...` only dies there. I checked that half through the registry in the test, not with a full run.\n\nNot a duplicate as far as I can tell: #53072 / #53124 cover `vllm serve --headless` only, and #52026 changes the module name plugins are imported under, not where they are imported.\n\nAI assistance was used to find and prepare this change.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [ ] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [ ] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [ ] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [ ] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [ ] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n",
